{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794320327255,"sessionID":"ses_e3a36c4b4ffeLccYDH8fxc3WFh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_5nd9csw8ycan2twseay9kk1k","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && /tmp/venv/bin/python -m py_compile backend/app.py && echo python-ok && sed -n '1,30p' README.md && sed -n '13,22p' Dockerfile","timeout":20000},"output":"python-ok\n# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed directly when present. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n    PORT=8000\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY backend/requirements.txt backend/requirements.lock* backend/\nRUN if [ -f backend/requirements.lock ]; then \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.lock; \\\n    else \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt; \\\n    fi\nCOPY backend/ backend/\nCOPY --from=frontend /app/frontend/dist frontend/dist\n","metadata":{"output":"python-ok\n# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed directly when present. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n    PORT=8000\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY backend/requirements.txt backend/requirements.lock* backend/\nRUN if [ -f backend/requirements.lock ]; then \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.lock; \\\n    else \\\n      pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt; \\\n    fi\nCOPY backend/ backend/\nCOPY --from=frontend /app/frontend/dist frontend/dist\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && /tmp/venv/bin/python -m py_compile backend/app.py && echo python-ok && sed -n '1,30p' README.md && sed -n '13,22p' Dockerfile","time":{"start":1794320327150,"end":1794320327236}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c5d361e0001iSeOBtbDyv1J69","sessionID":"ses_e3a36c4b4ffeLccYDH8fxc3WFh","messageID":"msg_1c5d3291b00120gi2YijBJ4V24"}}
